  "question": {
    "text": "Two coherent plane light waves of equal amplitude makes a small angle $\\alpha(< < 1)$ with each other. They fall almost normally on a screen. If $\\lambda$ is the wavelength of light waves, the fringe width $\\Delta x$ of interference patterns of the two sets of waves on the screen is",
    "image": null
